WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.772
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 3: Fun and Games.

2
00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:10.936
In this unit you will learn the words for games
and play, like bounce, roll, throw and catch.

3
00:00:11.016 --> 00:00:19.178
You will name the parts of your body, and learn the
words that say where something is — on, under, next to,

4
00:00:19.258 --> 00:00:20.333
left and right.

5
00:00:20.413 --> 00:00:27.189
You will play simple games, try a game from
another country, and listen to a funny story.

6
00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:31.811
You will also hear the short 'u' sound in sun, fun and duck.

7
00:00:31.891 --> 00:00:34.893
Learn by playing — that is the best way.

8
00:00:34.973 --> 00:00:41.363
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:41.443 --> 00:00:49.747
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
act out ball actions (bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit).

10
00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:55.669
You will also name parts of the body
(hand, foot, ear, nose, shoulder, head…)

11
00:00:55.749 --> 00:01:01.976
You will also say where something is (on,
under, next to) and show left and right.

12
00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:04.822
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:04.902 --> 00:01:10.111
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: bounce, roll, throw, catch, hit, run.

14
00:01:10.191 --> 00:01:15.273
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:15.353 --> 00:01:19.288
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:19.368 --> 00:01:24.266
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Big Ball and Talk about Fun and Games.

17
00:01:24.346 --> 00:01:25.127
Read actively.

18
00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:29.368
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:33.363
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:33.443 --> 00:01:37.390
The first language focus is Tell what you can do at play.

21
00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.005
Choose a game action you are good at.

22
00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:43.255
Say the sentence, then show it with your body.

23
00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:50.957
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:54.863
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:54.943 --> 00:01:59.154
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:02.420
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.814
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:05.894 --> 00:02:07.350
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:13.961
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:14.041 --> 00:02:17.167
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:17.247 --> 00:02:24.580
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
